                <pb facs="0299" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9013: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Counselor of Embassy in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-29T16:00:00-04:00">July 29, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>146. Your 308, July 28, 7 a.m., paragraph 3. Having given this matter careful
                    consideration in the light of all the information available and of action taken
                    in the interval, the Department is of the opinion that the express action you
                    suggest need not be taken at this time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
